# No trailing slash: a symlinked node_modules — pnpm, a shared store, a
# monorepo — is not matched by `node_modules/`, and an untracked entry makes the
# build read the worktree as dirty and quietly produce a dev build instead of
# the release the tag names.
node_modules
.output
.wxt
*.log

# Internal working files: agent configuration, Web Store notes, the prompt
# benchmark corpus and its transcripts. This repository is what a user reads to
# verify what they installed and what a contributor reads to change it; none of
# that is either. They are versioned all the same, in a second git history over
# the same working tree (`.git-internal`, private — see CLAUDE.md).
#
# This list and `.git-internal/info/exclude` MUST stay in step: a path named in
# neither is published by accident, a path named here alone is versioned
# nowhere.
.git-internal
CLAUDE.md
CHROMEWEBSTORE.md
skills-lock.json
docs/
fixtures/
.agents/
.claude/

# The release workflow explains itself by pointing at CLAUDE.md, which is not
# published. It stays internal until it reads for someone who cannot open that
# file — and until then, no tag triggers a release.
.github/
